WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.500
A political

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.202
bombshell in North Carolina

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.603
tonight, State Representative

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:04.471
Trisha Cauthen,

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.339
who won by 20 points

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.641
as a Democrat in her blue district

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.442
last fall,

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.211
announcing at a press conference today

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:14.247
she's now a Republican.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.449
As long as I have been a Democrat.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.084
The Democrats

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.820
have tried to be a big tent.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.890
But this now where we are modern day

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.592
Democratic Party

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:28.328
has become unrecognizable to me

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.363
and to so many others

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:33.099
throughout this state and this country.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.869
I'm no longer a Democrat,

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.304
but I remain a public servant.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.574
That is what I am called to do.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.777
The party that best represents

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:46.112
me and my principles

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.614
and what's best for North

00:00:47.614 --> 00:00:50.250
Carolina is the Republican Party.

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.420
Her switch means the Republicans now

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.854
have a veto proof

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.589
majority in the state House

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:57.690
and the Senate.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:58.792
I'm back now with our panel.

00:00:58.792 --> 00:00:59.459
Also joining us,

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.294
we have comedian and Princeton fellow

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.762
Maysoon Zayid.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.130
Great to have you.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.131
Lauren, this is a fine.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.032
How do you do for her

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.168
voters who just voted for her

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.302
a few months ago?

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.236
First of all,

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:13.239
she was endorsed and paid for.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.008
Her campaign was supported

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.976
and underwritten by organizations

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.011
like Emily's List

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:19.679
and the Human Rights Campaign.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.814
She represents a district

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:22.682
that is over 60%,

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.451
and she was a long time Democrat.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.718
A long time Democrat.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.521
I mean, this feels just so.

00:01:28.555 --> 00:01:29.055
I mean, listen,

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:29.889
people are entitled

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:31.624
to change their views, and I.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.859
I would never

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:33.660
you know,

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.361
I would never criticize that

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.796
in another kind of situation.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.731
But she literally was just elected.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.532
And she was elected

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:41.434
based on a set of understandings

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.902
with her constituents

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:43.870
and a

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:46.539
career of service on the Democratic side.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:48.241
And in a state like North Carolina,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.477
where the margins are so critical,

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.245
this is devastating for that community.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.948
There is no recall option in this state

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:57.150
that the voters cannot get her back,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.252
even though she completely mis

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.286
misrepresented herself.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.087
And I think to me,

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:01.754
this is a lot

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.089
like the George Santos case.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:04.591
I mean, she completely pulled the wool

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.092
over the eyes on her constituents.

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.460
We're not talking about like a year

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.628
long evolution.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:09.896
It was like three months.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:11.664
She clearly had this plan.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.266
Mason Here is what the governor

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:15.135
of North Carolina, a Democrat, says

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.469
is now on the line.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.538
Representative Collins votes on women's

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:20.607
reproductive freedom, election laws,

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.308
LGBTQ rights.

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:24.043
Strong public schools will determine

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.112
the direction of the state we love.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:26.880
It's hard to believe

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.747
she would abandon

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.282
these long held principles,

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.084
as she should still vote

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.418
the way she has always said

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.453
she would vote

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.187
when these issues

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.088
arise, regardless

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:36.523
of her party affiliation.

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:38.291
She's not going to vote the way

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.025
that you said

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:39.726
she was going to vote

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.361
because she's not even right

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.363
representing her constituents.

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.130
So you're talking

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:45.498
about changing your mind.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.833
You can change your mind.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:47.634
But honestly,

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.101
I think

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:50.403
if you are elected as a Democrat,

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.238
you have to serve as a Democrat.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.940
I know it's a little fun thing

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.440
where we are

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:54.841
all like,

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.943
Oh, man, she's going to switch parties

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.645
and then all the majority switches

00:02:58.645 --> 00:02:59.913
and all the rules switch.

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:02.282
That's not representative.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.484
You're representing the people.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:06.653
You're not representing yourself.

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:08.922
You were voted in as a Democrat.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.256
You could actually vote.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.559
However you want as a Democrat.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.661
You could vote against every bill

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.129
you said you would support

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:18.264
by giving them a super majority.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:19.732
That's got to be fraud.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:20.900
It's got to be a plot.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:22.335
And either it's a long game

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:23.369
for ten years

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:26.072
or three months ago, somebody found fault

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.241
because you don't just wake up one day

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:30.877
and go, no, I don't want equality.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.145
I want women to die.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:33.213
She blamed emojis.

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.180
That's my favorite part.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:34.881
I'm not really.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.015
What like to talk about that?

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.650
Here she is. Here's what she says.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.285
Was just a bridge too far.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:40.119
This is what the tipping

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:43.923
point was for her and why she switched.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.025
One of the absolute worst moments,

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.460
which was deal breaker.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.329
A turning point for me

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:51.464
was when I was criticized

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:53.466
for using the American flag

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.501
and the praying hands emoji

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.537
on all my social media platforms

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.439
and even on the back of

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:02.308
different vehicles that I have.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.543
I really could not believe

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.711
that was the conversation

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.913
that was happening at that time,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.150
and I was deeply offended to say that

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.252
that is wrong

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:15.388
and not to be able to show off the flag

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.423
because the others

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.525
hijack it for something else.

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:22.161
Why are we at

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:25.531
this place in politics,

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.266
Jessica?

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.233
I mean, I would just say

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:29.202
I'm incredibly skeptical.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.170
That is a reason to change parties.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.071
I would also

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.806
imagine there are plenty of people

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.108
who are Christian

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:36.776
or who like an American flag,

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:38.778
who are Democrats in North Carolina.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:39.779
I can't believe

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.848
that's like a party decision

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.216
kind of thing.

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.118
I do think I mean, her constituents

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.819
must be incredibly concerned

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:47.687
because Republicans

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:49.789
now do have this veto proof majority.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:50.957
And that means that all

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:51.591
these issues

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.259
that she ran on, publicly ran

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.994
on, was endorsed by Emily's List.

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.596
Those are all at threat.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:57.163
And so I think

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.631
they must be incredibly scared

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.832
about what this means.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:00.600
John, your thoughts?

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:00.867
Yeah,

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:02.268
she's not the only Democrat

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:03.569
who's concerned about the party

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:04.971
being unrecognizable.

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:06.572
You know, Joe Manchin is concerned.

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:07.240
And the fact is

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.775
the Democratic Party is not so much

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:09.575
the Liberal Party.

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:11.477
It's become an illiberal party

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:12.512
that's increasingly

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:13.880
intolerant of different views,

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:15.882
you know, woke, cancel culture and so on.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:17.950
I mean, Joe Biden is hardly Mr. Woke.

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:18.518
Well,

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:19.252
yeah, but here's

00:05:19.252 --> 00:05:20.620
that's that's actually a good example

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.055
because look at Donald Trump

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:23.089
and Joe Biden.

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:23.956
Since 2016,

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:24.991
I've argued that Donald

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:26.526
Trump represents the GOP's

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.994
personality crisis.

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:30.296
Donald Trump is not policy.

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.198
There is no Trumpism apart from the man.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:32.999
Whereas

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.634
and Trump plagiarized Reagan

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.668
and all of his policies,

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:38.071
whereas Joe Biden is stealing ideas

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.272
from Bernie Sanders.

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:40.873
So Biden actually

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:41.641
Biden shows

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.675
how the Democratic Party is

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:43.843
veers to the left

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:45.712
on energy and climate issues.

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:47.880
The public is with the Republican view

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.249
on H.R. one, the Lower Energy Cost Act.

00:05:50.616 --> 00:05:52.018
They want permitting reform.

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:53.152
They want more nuclear energy.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:54.420
They want an all of the above energy.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.121
But in terms of.

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:56.422
They can't get that here.

00:05:57.657 --> 00:05:58.091
Hold on.

00:05:58.091 --> 00:05:58.691
Hold on.

00:05:58.891 --> 00:05:59.625
She's not.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:00.727
But in terms of this,

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:03.162
do you think that this particular woman,

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:04.330
Tricia Gotham.

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:07.100
Do you think that she has misled

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:08.167
her voters?

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.302
And do you think they have a right

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:10.470
to be angry today?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.437
I think I think

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:12.872
voters always have a right to be angry.

00:06:12.872 --> 00:06:13.172
I think

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:14.640
I think any politician has a right

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.408
to change their mind

00:06:15.408 --> 00:06:16.776
or change their affiliation.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:17.910
And those politicians

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:18.811
will be held accountable

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.012
in the next election.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:20.313
That's

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.181
how our system of government works.

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:25.084
But but to to not acknowledge,

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:25.885
if you're a Democrat,

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:28.020
that your party has has problems,

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.222
you're not dealing with reality.

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:29.989
Well, she didn't say that.

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:31.724
And I hear you, but she didn't say that.

00:06:31.724 --> 00:06:32.792
She said it was because

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.327
people were criticizing her

00:06:34.327 --> 00:06:35.595
for the American flag

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:36.629
and praying hands emoji.

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:37.430
And I just don't know.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.865
I wish she had said

00:06:38.865 --> 00:06:39.465
and explained

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.200
if she meant on social media

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.302
or her colleagues in the state house.

00:06:43.336 --> 00:06:44.504
So I don't know what she means

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:46.506
when she says people are sorry. Go ahead.

00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:47.039
No, please.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:47.240
No.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.441
I also just, like

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.243
have to push back on all of this

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:50.977
and say

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.178
I'm looking at a woman

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:54.280
who crying about flags and emojis

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.416
when we are women of color

00:06:56.416 --> 00:06:57.750
living in this country,

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.952
getting death threats every single day,

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:01.954
being told, we don't belong here,

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:02.889
I'm a muslim.

00:07:02.889 --> 00:07:04.824
You want to talk about praying hands?

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:06.559
I've lived through a presidency

00:07:06.559 --> 00:07:09.195
that wanted to ban my family and ban me.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.563
So when we talk about,

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:11.731
oh, it's not a big tent

00:07:11.731 --> 00:07:13.366
and it doesn't resemble

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:14.000
I don't know,

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.469
I feel pretty comfortable playing safe

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:17.970
around the Democratic Party.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:18.438
And I

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:19.505
don't feel

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:22.775
Americans safe or welcome around the GOP.

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:25.211
So even though I feel her being like,

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.613
Oh, they didn't like my bumper sticker,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.549
that's why you're abandoning

00:07:29.549 --> 00:07:30.716
women's, right?

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:31.584
That comment describes

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:33.686
why Donald Trump is such a toxic person.

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:35.254
Because the American idea

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:36.022
is the opposite

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:36.456
of everything

00:07:36.456 --> 00:07:37.323
you just described

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:38.624
is that our founders

00:07:38.624 --> 00:07:40.259
believe of freedom of religion

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:41.627
and that you're your rights

00:07:41.627 --> 00:07:42.328
and your dignity

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:43.162
does not depend

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:44.764
on your religious

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:46.232
affiliation, your ethnicity.

00:07:46.232 --> 00:07:47.433
That's the American idea.

00:07:47.433 --> 00:07:48.601
That's what our country was founded.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.069
The problem in North Carolina

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:51.170
and in many states around

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:52.772
the country is that it has become a

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.040
it is essentially a tyranny

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.274
of the minority.

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:57.310
You have a state legislature

00:07:57.477 --> 00:07:59.745
that has supermajorities

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:01.180
of Republicans in places

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.782
where actually there is much closer

00:08:02.782 --> 00:08:03.616
to a 5050

00:08:03.616 --> 00:08:05.852
or a 4060 split among the voters.

00:08:06.085 --> 00:08:07.787
It's not just there. It's in Kansas.

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:08.721
It's in Wisconsin.

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:10.022
It's all over the country

00:08:10.022 --> 00:08:10.756
where voters

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:11.357
and by the way,

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:12.191
even Republican

00:08:12.191 --> 00:08:12.859
voters are saying

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:15.261
they do not want extreme abortion ban.

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:16.262
It is

00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:17.930
the highest number measured

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.799
in American history.

00:08:19.799 --> 00:08:21.200
63% of Americans

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:21.934
